<title>RUSSIA: Russian 1996 automobile output up four pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Russian 1996 automobile output up four pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia produced 868,000 automobiles in 1996, a rise of four percent on a year earlier, the State Statitstics Committee said. It released the following data:</p>
<p>    RUSSIAN VEHICLE OUTPUT     Jan-Dec'96 Jan-Nov'96 Jan-Dec'95</p>
<p>    total production automobiles  868,000    792,000    835,000</p>
<p>    yr/yr pct change			 +4	   +2	   +5</p>
<p>    total production trucks	 136,000    123,000	  n/a</p>
<p>    yr/yr pct change			 -9	  -10	  n/a</p>
<p>    total production buses	   38,200     34,700	  n/a</p>
<p>    yr/yr pct change			 -4	   -4	  n/a</p>
<p>					     Dec '96   Nov '96   Dec '95</p>
<p>    mth/mth pct change autos	    +4	 -18	  -7</p>
<p>    yr/yr pct change		     +22	 +10	 -13</p>
<p>    mth/mth pct change trucks	   +0.8	+7	 +30</p>
<p>    yr/yr pct change			+5	 +28	 -32</p>
<p>    mth/mth pct change buses	   +12	 -27	 +41</p>
<p>    yr/yr pct change			-6	 +18	 -40</p>
<p>					    mth/mth</p>
<p>					  pct change by</p>
<p>					  manufacturer</p>
<p>    GAZ				     +3</p>
<p>    UAZ				    +10</p>
<p>    AvtoVAZ				 +3</p>
<p>    KamAZ				  +12</p>
<p>    Zil				    +11</p>
<p>    Izhmash				 +9</p>
<p>The Committee that automobile and truck production at AO KamAZ had risen 0.8 percent in 1996 on 1995, output at AO GAZ had risen four percent and that output at AvtoVAZ had risen 12 percent.</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
